                                            <msContents>
                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Pentateuch</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-12-item-1">
                                                    <locus from="2v" to="71v"/>
                                                    <title>Genesis</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <incipit>
                                                        <quote xml:lang="ar">في البدء خلق الله السماء و الارض و كانت الارض غير منظورةو غير مستعدة و الظلمة على الغمر</quote>
                                                    </incipit>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-12-item-2">
                                                    <locus from="72v" to="131v"/>
                                                    <title>Exodus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-12-item-3">
                                                    <locus from="132v" to="175v"/>
                                                    <title>Leviticus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-12-item-4">
                                                    <locus from="176v" to="236"/>
                                                    <title>Numbers</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-12-item-5">
                                                    <locus from="237v" to="289v"/>
                                                    <title>Deuteronomy</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Translated from the Septuagint.</note>
                                                </msItem>
                                            </msContents>
                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_80ccbabe6058e69a35b897): 13 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 260 × 180 mm. Cahiers numérotés en lettres arabes à 10 fol. Gloses marginales. Papier oriental. 290 fol. (f. 1, 72, 132, 176, 236 v-237, 290 v laissés en blanc). Folioté en chiffres coptes. Écriture orientale (Égypte). Texte vocalisé. — Titres en lettres dorées. Enluminures faites de dessins géométriques dorés sur fond bleu (f. 1 v-2) ; titres écrits en coufique dans des sarlohs dorés sur fond bleu (f. 2 v-3, 72v-73, 132 v-133, 176 v-177, 237 v-238, 289 v-290). 385 × 265 mm. Reliure orientale à rabat, basane rouge. Médaillons, fleurons et coins estampés à chaud.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">290 folios (ff. 1, 72, 132, 176, 236v-237, 290v blank); foliated in Coptic numerals</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">385</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">265</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                        <condition>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Exceptional communication, subject to authorization by the director of the department on motivated request.</note>
                                                        </condition>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">13 lines per page. Gatherings numbered in Arabic letters, 10 folios per gathering. Marginal glosses.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="13" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">260</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">180</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Egyptian. Text vocalized.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <decoDesc>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Titles in gold letters.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Illuminations of gold geometric drawings on blue ground at ff. 1v-2.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Titles written in Kufic in golden sarlohs on blue ground at ff. 2v-3, 72v-73, 132v-133, 176v-177, 237v-238, 289v-290.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                </decoDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental binding with flap, red sheepskin; medallions, fleurons and corners stamped in gold.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_80ccbabe6058e69a35b897): Pentateuque. Date described in the BnF catalogue: 1353.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Anonymous notice.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <acquisition>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Sent by the abbé d’Orvalle in 1749.</note>
                                                </acquisition>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" when="1353">1353</origDate>
                                                    <p>Copy made by Ǧirǧis, son of the priest Abū al-Mufaḍḍal, and completed on 28 Abīb 1069 of the Martyrs (f. 290).</p>
                                                    <p>A note at f. 290 states that the text was collated against Greek, Hebrew and Coptic in AH 754 / 1353 according to a manuscript written by the priest Ibn Kabar.</p>
                                                </origin>
                                            </history>
